      "message": "No, that is the right process.\n\nSome types have become declaration-only. `abitidy` then prunes away anything unreachable resulting in other types vanishing altogether.\n\nWe still don\u0027t know why libabigail sometimes picks up only declarations and no definitions of a given struct. There are more details from https://sourceware.org/bugzilla/show_bug.cgi?id\u003d26646#c5 onwards.\n\nThere is a known workaround (as mentioned there), but it is expensive as it adds 90s to `abidw` running time on a fast machine.\n\nFTR the `vmlinux{3,4}` mentioned in the bug correspond to the LKGB and presubmit build for aosp/1925903, respectively.",
